  "body": "PATCH `4.23.0` → `4.23.1`. The previous guide was thin where it mattered and **wrong in three places**.\n\n## Corrections — checked against the code, not assumed\n\n**1. The auth token is not \"any value\".** I wrote that any non-empty token works. It isn't true: `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` ships as `freecc` in `.env.example` and is compared in constant time against the bearer token the agent sends (`dependencies.py:71-78`). A mismatch is a 401. It only *looks* optional because the code default is empty — which disables auth entirely.\n\n**2. Claude Code is configured via `settings.json`, not shell exports.** I recommended `export ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=...`. The settings file **wins over exported variables**, so that advice would silently do nothing for anyone who already had `~/.claude/settings.json`.\n\n**3. The proxy does not bind to loopback.** `host` defaults to `0.0.0.0`, so it is reachable across the network; only the Admin UI is loopback-restricted. The old text said the opposite — the wrong direction to be wrong about a security property.\n\n## Real tutorials\n\n**Claude Code (CLI)** — the exact `env` block, both platform paths, the merge-don't-replace warning, verifying with `/status`, and the model picker screenshot.\n\n**Claude Desktop** — five steps with the README's screenshots: *Help → Troubleshooting → Enable Developer Mode*, *Developer → Configure Third-Party Inference…*, the full field table, test-before-restart, and the two things to expect afterwards (ignorable warning dialog, local sessions only).\n\n## Also added\n\nHow it works with the architecture diagram · validation-failure table (the 404-means-model-id case catches people constantly) · local provider base URLs · model tier advice · expanded web search · how to read the cache columns including why NIM shows none · rotation · deferred Windows update · a security section covering what binds where.\n\n**15 embedded images, 14 sections, ~4,000 words.**\n\n## In-dashboard Guide corrected too\n\nThe Guide tab shipped in 4.23.0 repeated all three errors. Fixed to match.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\nmissing referenced files : none\nbroken anchors           : none\nimages embedded          : 15\nguide view present       : True\nTOC anchors / headings   : 9 / 9\n```\n\nFull suite passes except the 14 failures that also fail on unmodified `main`.\n\n## Residual risks\n\nBoth documents are static and will drift as options change — nothing enforces that the settings they mention still exist. The `.env.example` contract test covers the web search catalog only.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
