    "message": "docs: rewrite the usage guide with real tutorials, and correct three errors\n\nThe previous guide was thin where it mattered most and wrong in three places\nthat would have cost someone an evening.\n\nCorrections, all checked against the code rather than assumed:\n\n- The auth token is not \"any non-empty value\". ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN ships as\n  freecc in .env.example and is compared in constant time against the bearer\n  token the agent sends; a mismatch is a 401. It only reads as optional because\n  the code default is empty, which disables auth entirely.\n- Claude Code is configured through ~/.claude/settings.json, not shell exports.\n  The settings file wins, so the exported variables the old guide recommended\n  would silently do nothing for anyone who already had that file.\n- The proxy does not bind to loopback. host defaults to 0.0.0.0, so it is\n  reachable across the network; only the admin UI is loopback-restricted. The\n  old text told people the opposite, which is the wrong direction to be wrong\n  about a security property.\n\nBoth Claude Code and Claude Desktop now have step-by-step tutorials with the\nscreenshots the README already carries: the exact settings.json block, how to\nverify with /status, and for Desktop the Help -> Troubleshooting -> Enable\nDeveloper Mode path, the Configure Third-Party Inference dialog, the full field\ntable, and the test-before-restart step.\n\nAlso added: how it works with the architecture diagram, a table for reading\nvalidation failures (the 404-means-model-id case catches people constantly),\nlocal provider base URLs, model tier advice, expanded web search, how to read\nthe cache columns including why NVIDIA NIM shows no caching, rotation, the\ndeferred Windows update, and a security section covering the bind addresses.\n\nThe in-dashboard Guide carried the same three errors and has been corrected to\nmatch.\n\nVerified: every referenced asset exists, every anchor resolves, the served\nindex.html still carries the guide with nine sections and nine anchors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
